  "content": "<p>Check your understanding of this lesson. Your answers aren't recorded.</p>\n<multiple-choice question=\"Which change gives a shallower depth of field (more background blur)?\" single-option=\"\" randomize=\"\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"A lower f-stop (a wider aperture)\" data-correct=\"true\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"A higher f-stop\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"Moving the camera farther from the subject\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"Increasing the render resolution\">\n</multiple-choice>\n<true-false-question question=\"A longer focal length (telephoto) compresses the sense of depth between foreground and background.\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"True\" data-correct=\"true\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"False\">\n</true-false-question>\n<self-check title=\"Think it through\">\n  <p slot=\"question\">How would you use the rule of thirds to frame a product shot?</p>\n  <p>Place the product, or its most important feature, on one of the third lines or intersections, leave space in the direction it faces, and keep any horizon on a third line rather than in the middle, unless you want a deliberately symmetrical shot.</p>\n</self-check>\n"
